sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant I as Interviewer
    participant C as Candidate
    participant B as Board
    I->>C: here is the problem
    C->>I: functional requirements — what must it do?
    C->>I: non-functional — scale, latency, consistency, availability
    C->>B: core entities and the API between them
    C->>B: back-of-envelope numbers before any boxes
    C->>B: the standard request path — client, edge, service, cache, store
    I->>C: go deep on one part
    C->>B: partitioning, hot keys, the read/write split
    C->>B: what breaks first at 10x, and which rung of the ladder you climb
    Note over C,B: requirements to numbers to design to deep dive — in that order, every time
